      "The diagnosis of ST-elevation myocardial infarction is made on the ECG and clinical presentation; no biomarker is needed and waiting for one only wastes myocardium. Reperfusion should occur as soon as possible: if primary PCI cannot be delivered within 90-120 minutes of first medical contact, as in this rural scenario, fibrinolysis should be given within 30 minutes of first medical contact (after checking contraindications) as part of a pharmaco-invasive strategy, with transfer for angiography afterwards. Aspirin 300 mg chewed, analgesia, and discussion with the receiving service or retrieval coordinator should occur simultaneously.",
